{:edb/db-before-t 2029 :edb/db-after-t 2030 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535342 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:27:10.620Z" 13194139535342 true] [17592186152106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344792 13194139535342 true] [17592186152106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186344796 13194139535342 true] [17592186283254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344795 13194139535342 true] [17592186344792 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344793 13194139535342 true] [17592186344792 1089 "q-281121" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344792 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535342 true] [17592186344792 1100 "Consider the line $y=2x+1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-3.$" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344792 1113 #uuid "f75b74c5-e95f-51fa-9efd-e0ac511581a1" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344792 1145 "First, notice that the line $y=2x+1$ passes through the points $A(0,1)$ and $B(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(2,-1)$ and ${B}^{′}(7,-2).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+1 & =\\frac{-2+1}{7-2}(x-2) \\\\ y+1 & =-\\frac{1}{5}(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =-\\frac{1}{5}(x-2) \\\\ 5y+5 & =-x+2 \\\\ x+5y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344793 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344794 13194139535342 true] [17592186344793 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535342 true] [17592186344793 1041 "field-1" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344793 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344794 13194139535342 true] [17592186344793 1110 #uuid "26a17d43-112b-5745-a663-0ba1628c09f4" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344794 1034 "x+5y" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344794 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535342 true] [17592186344794 1111 #uuid "d9453693-2f6b-53df-b1b7-0d188b90f75c" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344795 1034 "x+2y" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344795 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535342 true] [17592186344795 1111 #uuid "7573ae91-a983-5b17-bc51-6ecefd2f108b" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344796 1017 #edb/ref 17592186344797 13194139535342 true] [17592186344796 1089 "q-77771" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344796 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535342 true] [17592186344796 1100 "Consider the line $y=-2x+3$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344796 1113 #uuid "9c181e4f-0f89-544f-856a-3ad22207819d" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344796 1145 "First, notice that the line $y=-2x+3$ passes through the points $U(0,3)$ and $V(1,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $U$ and $V$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${U}^{′}(-6,-3)$ and ${V}^{′}(-2,2).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${U}^{′}$ and ${V}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-3) & =\\frac{2-(-3)}{-2-(-6)}(x-(-6)) \\\\ y+3 & =\\frac{5}{4}(x+6) \\\\ 4y+12 & =5x+30 \\\\ 5x-4y+18 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344798 13194139535342 true] [17592186344797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344799 13194139535342 true] [17592186344797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344800 13194139535342 true] [17592186344797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344801 13194139535342 true] [17592186344797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186344802 13194139535342 true] [17592186344797 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535342 true] [17592186344797 1041 "selection" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344797 1104 #edb/ref 17592186344801 13194139535342 true] [17592186344797 1110 #uuid "7ca0d668-1b87-5b28-9a5a-0445ee3ebc5d" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344798 1034 "4x-5y+18=0" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344798 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535342 true] [17592186344798 1111 #uuid "fcc10ca3-1af7-50c4-b3f7-a50aa55766ef" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344799 1034 "5x+2y+18=0" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344799 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535342 true] [17592186344799 1111 #uuid "31c67c8a-3dce-55e1-95fb-f6640a6a437d" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344800 1034 "5x-2y+8=0" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344800 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535342 true] [17592186344800 1111 #uuid "e371970f-3e17-581f-b25c-f6e3bcb847e8" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344801 1034 "5x-4y+18=0" 13194139535342 true] [17592186344801 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535342 true] [17592186344801 1111 #uuid "2a332799-bf6f-5f8e-a569-4d3d92f6125e" 13194139535342 true] [175921